title: 'Mod playbooks, checkpoint 11: S1 committed; Arky''s naming and versioning design; integration plan'
summary: |-
  S1 is b296fed5 on feat/gnomon-desk-s1, rebased on 5a40e28a:
  - desk-guidance is a composite single block (the voice-only hash is unchanged)
  - offer-router has D1 human-only, one decision per offer
  - mcp-passthrough fails closed on a non-absolute command
  - the override store is in the home dir (0600) with a root-class card
  - gnomon desk stats
  - 2626 tests
  - Gap: Claude Code spawns the MCP servers, so Gnomon cannot enforce shell:false; override env values land in mcp.json. Aegis is reviewing.

  S2 is e3d7b151 (Aegis fixes: automate-this dropped, brain writes confirmed first, fail-closed launch).

  Arky's design, refining the founder-approved proposal:
  - events stay modns.<publisher>.<name>.* (the kernel owns mod.*)
  - MCP server gm_<pub>_<name> (underscore, unambiguous), with a gx_<name14>_<hash8> fallback, under the 64-char tool-name cap
  - folders declare a publisher, shown unverified
  - first-party env prefix is <NAME>_ (GNOMON_ is denied)
  - Windows device names are reserved publishers
  - manifest:2 with a pure v1 upgrader; manifestHash is over the raw bytes; engines.gnomon is a restricted range; future majors are refused FORMAT
  - a fixed 3-name legacy alias table
  - one more clientApiId move inside the same reservation
  - request.offer.mute takes hsid (the kernel derives the repo, so it is unspoofable); unmuting from Settings is deferred

  Integration plan: once Aegis rules on S1, merge S0→S1→S2→S3 into feat/gnomon-desk-o1, then apply naming and versioning as S0b on top (avoiding rebase conflicts), then merge into feat/gnomon.
